  - `FAIL server/lib/spaces/gatekeeper-program.test.js > gatekeeper program`
  - `Error: the gatekeeper ended with 1: gatekeeper: listener error EADDRINUSE` at `gatekeeper-program.test.js:249`
- The next oc-review runs on main (2026-10-28T11:08Z, 12:18Z, 12:19Z) passed, so this is intermittent, matching a port race rather than a code regression.
- Dedup: no open or closed issue mentions this failure (`gatekeeper` search returns only the unrelated #25 handoff).

## Acceptance criteria

- [ ] `gatekeeper-program.test.js` no longer relies on probe-and-release ports for the spawned gatekeeper child: either the child retries/rebinds on `EADDRINUSE` (e.g. the test respawns with fresh ports a bounded number of times), or the ports are held by the parent until the child has bound them, or an equivalent race-free scheme.
- [ ] The same treatment is considered for the identical `freePort` pattern in `server/lib/opencode/self-handoff-process.test.js`, or a comment records why that file's usage cannot collide.
- [ ] The gatekeeper suite passes repeatedly (e.g. 10 consecutive runs of the file, and a full-suite run) with no `EADDRINUSE` failure.

