## Bug

`readLocalZip` in `packages/web/server/lib/guests/install.js` judges its 20 MiB archive cap on a pre-read stat of the path, then reads the file by path whole:

```js
// install.js:26
const MAX_ZIP_BYTES = 20 * 1024 * 1024;
// install.js:171-181
const readLocalZip = async (filePath) => {
  try {
    const stat = await fs.stat(filePath);
    if (!stat.isFile() || stat.size > MAX_ZIP_BYTES) {
      return null;
    }
    return await fs.readFile(filePath);
  } catch {
    return null;
  }
};
```

The stat and the read are two separate by-path operations, so the gate judges a different file than the read consumes:

- A file **grown after the stat** (or swapped for a larger one) is buffered whole past `MAX_ZIP_BYTES` and handed to `installGuestFromZipBuffer` / `extractZipBuffer` — the cap the module's own header assigns to this path (`install.js:282`: "path and URL installs stop at `MAX_ZIP_BYTES`") never applies to the bytes actually read.
- A **FIFO swapped in after the stat** passes the `isFile` judge (which already ran) and blocks `fs.readFile` forever — there is no `O_NONBLOCK` open and no deadline on this path, so the install request never settles.

There are in fact two stats before the read: `installGuestFromPath` stats the path at `install.js:303-304` to decide it is a zip file, then `readLocalZip` stats it again at `:173` — two TOCTOU windows instead of one.

This is the stat-then-read-by-path shape the shared bounded reader exists to prevent (`packages/web/server/lib/shared/bounded-file-read.js`: open once with `O_NONBLOCK`, judge the handle, enforce the cap during the read). Its two siblings in this very module already do it correctly in spirit: the https download path (`requestHttpsPinned`, `install.js:195-245`) refuses an over-cap `Content-Length` up front and enforces `MAX_ZIP_BYTES` while streaming, chunk by chunk. Only the local-path reader judges before the read and never during it. Same residual class as #1730 (git status) and #1731 (cloudflared config), in a module those filings did not cover.

