The local-path install is a user-facing route (`POST /api/guests` install by path). The 20 MiB cap is the only bound between a path on disk and an in-memory buffer plus zip extraction; defeating it with a grow/swap between two syscalls means the bound is advisory. The FIFO variant wedges the install request indefinitely with no error surface. Both are exactly the failure modes the rest of this codebase has been systematically closing via the shared bounded reader.

